  "query_preview": "..\nAn active weather pattern will persist across the Marianas beginning\nthis evening through Saturday night before tapering down on Labor \nDay. A surface trough associated with Invest 97W to the west and a \ncol to the east places the region within an unsettled convergence \nzone. As seen on satellite, westerly flow is buckling against the \nfrontmost quadrants of the col, and as the col continues moving west-\nnorthwest, numerous showers and isolated thunderstorms with possible\nlocally heavy showers are expected Saturday and Saturday night, \npotentially heavier over Saipan and Tinian. Scatterometry depicts \nmoderate to fresh southwesterlies which will taper down to gentle to \nmoderate after tonight, with occasional convective gusts up to 25 mph\npossible. Scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms are forecasted\nthrough Labor Day, followed by a potential dry spell through the \nremainder of next week.",
